<title>USA: U.S. business loans rose $2.40 bln in Aug 21 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. business loans rose $2.40 bln in Aug 21 week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans on the books of U.S. commercial banks, excluding acceptances, rose $2.397 billion to $358.96 billion in the week ended Aug 21, the Federal Reserve said Friday.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $2.399 billion to $360.54 billion, the Fed said.</p>
